  "notes": [
    "hookTargets mirror required Stash gameplay capabilities for the linux-x86_64-direct-stash-detour backend; production manifests load with failClosed=false when the required target set is installed, while unsupported builds or missing symbols/targets still fail closed.",
    "The prompt-scoped target set includes uidToEntity, Language::get, and selectedEntity so selected-entity and hover-tooltip prompts can be scoped to framework Stash access points.",
    "Static readiness remains conservative for Stash: it proves 42 ready, 0 blocked, and 0 missing targets across 30 required symbols, not full player-facing scenario coverage.",
    "Runebound: Elixirs target notes now describe the fake-provider/live-hook contract: useItem, Item::getName, statGetSTR, and statGetDEX detours are expected to install for the live pass; host-authoritative drop generation, metadata, sidecar state, and multiplayer metadata are exposed through the dedicated Runebound live install report rather than claimed as Steam-ready inventory injection; unsupported builds still fail closed."
  ],
